<title>UNITED NATIONS: Iraq oil-for-food terms need to reopen-US envoy.</title>
<headline>Iraq oil-for-food terms need to reopen-US envoy.</headline>
<dateline>UNITED NATIONS 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>United States envoy to the United Nations Edward Gnehm said on Tuesday that the May 20 oil-for-food accord with Iraq needs to be reopened in the wake of recent military action by Baghdad.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a matter of going back to the MOU (memorandum of understanding) and looking at it,&quot; Gnehm said. &quot;It was a designed program and those conditions don't exist any more.&quot;</p>
<p>Gnehm said he could not offer an estimate on how long implementation of the oil-for-food deal is likely to remain on hold, saying that would be decided by Saddam Hussein's actions. &quot;It could be months and months,&quot; Gnehm said.</p>
</text>
